{"id": "EUVD-2026-82181", "enisaUuid": "856c7abc-ca11-3855-8765-00b8e8ac32a1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: bcm2835-unicam: Fix asc leaked in error/remove path\n\nv4l2_async_nf_add_fwnode_remote() allocates the asc, which is freed when\nv4l2_async_nf_cleanup() is called.\n\nCall v4l2_async_nf_cleanup() properly in the driver paths.\n\nDiscovered with kmemleak after rmmod:\n\nunreferenced object 0xffff000084526b80 (size 64):\n  comm \"modprobe\", pid 185, jiffies 4295013512\n  hex dump (first 32 bytes):\n    01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 e8 0d ff bf 00 00 ff ff  ................\n    40 83 bc 84 00 00 ff ff 60 83 bc 84 00 00 ff ff  @.......`.......\n  backtrace (crc ac584083):\n    [<00000000ffb081a7>] kmemleak_alloc+0x38/0x44\n    [<00000000d2fd9301>] __kmalloc+0x1b0/0x250\n    [<000000004dd5354d>] __v4l2_async_nf_add_fwnode+0x28/0x9c\n    [<0000000067587657>] __v4l2_async_nf_add_fwnode_remote+0x3c/0x64", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5479372db364c80bb6bd59f640f5c31de3984bab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c29cd408ef86e695acb2a5d4e00fa2f5695368d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de9be39cefda1ecd762e6a913665c01f7bb18100", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/253c9659e25131b0169f718e7d094ac1aa0d9279"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93071", "GHSA-m33f-v49h-44x7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09827dd9-89d2-3175-b873-ded5669432cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "392cd78d495f36c201eb5cc425b01017d493e094 <2c29cd408ef86e695acb2a5d4e00fa2f5695368d"}, {"id": "22e775ed-d3ab-38f9-91e4-5ff87de760a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3de3378e-f108-3085-819f-60713a6cf620", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {